module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Abelian.Projective.Resolution
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LocalCohomology.BitUniformityI.VanishingEquivalences
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LocalCohomology.BitUniformityII.UniformTorTransition
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Tor.Balancing
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Uniform vanishing conditions for the transitions between the quotients by the powers of an ideal

Let `I` be an ideal of a Noetherian ring `A` generated by at most `t` elements. There are a
threshold `N` and a shift `c`, depending only on `A`, `I` and `t`, such that for every `n ≥ N` the
surjection `A / I ^ n ↠ A / I ^ (n - c)` satisfies the equivalent conditions of
[Stacks, Tag 0G9V] in degree `e = t`: a lift to any pair of projective resolutions can be chosen
to vanish in all homological degrees above `t`, the induced maps on `Ext ^ i` vanish for `i > t`,
and the induced maps on `Tor _ i` vanish for `i > t`.

## Main results

All of the following live in the namespace `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityII`.

* `exists_uniform_extMapVanishesAbove_quotientFactor`: uniform vanishing of the maps induced on
  `Ext ^ i` for all `i > t`, which is condition (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0G9V].
* `exists_uniform_torMapVanishesAtSucc_quotientFactor`: the same conclusion in the form of
  vanishing of the map induced on `Tor _ (t + 1)`, which is condition (7).
* `exists_uniform_hasLiftVanishingAbove_quotientFactor`: the same conclusion in the form of a
  lift of the transition to any chosen pair of projective resolutions whose components vanish in
  homological degrees above `t`, which is condition (1).
* `exists_uniform_vanishingConditions_quotientFactor`: all seven conditions of
  [Stacks, Tag 0G9V] at once, for any chosen pair of projective resolutions.
* `exists_uniform_torMapVanishesAtSucc_quotientFactor_of_annihilator_level` and
  `exists_uniform_extMapVanishesAbove_quotientFactor_of_annihilator_level`: the same conclusions
  in degree `e` for any level `e` at which the uniform annihilation holds, with no bound on the
  number of generators of `I`.

## How the statements are proved

The source deduces [Stacks, Tag 0GA3] from [Stacks, Tag 0GA2] and [Stacks, Tag 0G9V], and so do
the three statements below. [Stacks, Tag 0GA2] is
`exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_le_annihilator_tor'`, which rests on the uniform
annihilation of [Stacks, Tag 0GA1], proved on the blowup of `Spec A` in `I` as
`exists_pow_le_annihilator_tor_quotient_pow_blowup`. Its conclusion is condition (7) of
[Stacks, Tag 0G9V] after the braiding of the two models of `Tor`, and conditions (3) and (1)
follow from (7) by the equivalence of all seven conditions for a finite module over a Noetherian
ring, `tfae_of_isNoetherianRing_of_finite`.

The two statements at an arbitrary level `e` take the uniform annihilation at that level as an
input, since it is what fixes the level `e`.

[Stacks, Tag 0GA4] is a remark with two halves. The first is the result of the paper [AHS] that
for a local ring the conclusion holds with `e = dim A`; it is obtained here from the uniform
annihilation at level `dim A`, carried as the hypothesis `hann`, and not proved from scratch.
That level is not reachable from [Stacks, Tag 0GA3] by counting generators, since an ideal of a
local ring need not be generated by `dim A` elements, and the conclusion at a smaller level is
the stronger statement: vanishing on `Tor _ (e + 1)` against every module gives vanishing on
`Tor _ (e' + 1)` against every module whenever `e ≤ e'`, by dimension shifting in the first
variable. What the reduction needs is that the descending induction of [Stacks, Tag 0GA2] runs
over the generators of `I` while the degree of its conclusion is fixed by the level of the
annihilation, so the two are independent. The second half of the remark asks whether
`e = cd(A, I)` works, in the direction suggested by [Stacks, Tag 0EH1]; the source answers that
it does not know, so there is nothing to state.

## Implementation notes

The transition is the canonical map `Submodule.factor` induced by `I ^ n ≤ I ^ (n - c)`, in the
spelling used by [Stacks, Tag 0GA2]. The conclusion of that lemma is the vanishing of the map
induced on the model of `Tor` which derives the second variable; condition (7) of
[Stacks, Tag 0G9V] is stated for the model which derives the first variable, and the two are
matched by the braiding isomorphism `torFlip_iso_Tor'`. Since `A` is Noetherian and `A / I ^ n`
is a finite `A`-module, all seven conditions of [Stacks, Tag 0G9V] are equivalent for the
transition, so each of the statements below implies the others.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GA3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GA3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GA4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GA4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G9V](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G9V)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GA1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GA1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GA2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GA2)
* [AHS]: I. Aberbach, A. Hosry, J. Striuli, *Uniform Artin-Rees bounds for syzygies*,
  Adv. Math. **285** (2015), 478-496, the paper cited by [Stacks, Tag 0GA4].
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory

universe u

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

namespace Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityII

noncomputable section

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]

/-- The canonical cochain projective resolution of a module is a projective resolution. -/
private instance isProjectiveResolution_of_π' (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) :
    CochainComplex.IsProjectiveResolution (ProjectiveResolution.of M).π' :=
  ⟨⟨0, inferInstance⟩, fun _ ↦ inferInstance⟩

/-- Transport the vanishing of the maps induced on the model of `Tor` which derives the second
variable to condition (7) of [Stacks, Tag 0G9V], stated for the model which derives the first
variable. -/
private theorem torMapVanishesAtSucc_of_tor_map_eq_zero
    {M M' : ModuleCat.{u} A} (f : M ⟶ M') (e : ℕ)
    (h : ∀ N : ModuleCat.{u} A, ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (e + 1)).obj N).map f = 0) :
    TorMapVanishesAtSucc f e := by
  intro N
  have hnat := NatTrans.congr_app ((torFlip_iso_Tor' (R := A) (e + 1)).hom.naturality f) N
  simp only [NatTrans.comp_app,
    show ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (e + 1)).flip.map f).app N = 0 from h N] at hnat
  exact ((((torFlip_iso_Tor' (R := A) (e + 1)).app M).app N).cancel_iso_hom_left _ _).1
    (by simpa using hnat.symm)

/-- Over a Noetherian ring, vanishing of `A / I ^ n ↠ A / I ^ (n - c)` on `Tor _ (e + 1)` gives
its vanishing on `Ext ^ i` for `i > e`. -/
private theorem extMapVanishesAbove_of_torMapVanishesAtSucc [IsNoetherianRing A]
    (I : Ideal A) (n c : ℕ) {e : ℕ}
    (h : TorMapVanishesAtSucc
      (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
        (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c)))) e) :
    ExtMapVanishesAbove
      (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
        (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c)))) e :=
  ((tfae_of_isNoetherianRing_of_finite
    (ProjectiveResolution.of (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ n))).π'
    (ProjectiveResolution.of (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ (n - c)))).π' _ e).out 7 3).1 h

/-! ### Stacks tag 0GA3 -/

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0GA3, condition (7) of Tag 0G9V.** Let `I = (g 0, …, g (t - 1))` be an
ideal of a Noetherian ring `A` generated by at most `t` elements. There are `N` and `c`,
depending only on `A`, `I` and `t`, such that for every `n ≥ N` the transition
`A / I ^ n ↠ A / I ^ (n - c)` induces the zero map on `Tor _ (t + 1)` against every module.

This is [Stacks, Tag 0GA2], `exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_le_annihilator_tor'`,
read through the braiding of the two models of `Tor`. -/
@[stacks 0GA3 "condition (7) of Tag 0G9V"]
theorem exists_uniform_torMapVanishesAtSucc_quotientFactor [IsNoetherianRing A]
    {I : Ideal A} {t : ℕ} (g : Fin t → A) (hg : I = Ideal.span (Set.range g)) :
    ∃ N c : ℕ, ∀ n : ℕ, N ≤ n →
      TorMapVanishesAtSucc
        (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c)))) t := by
  obtain ⟨N, c, h⟩ := exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_le_annihilator_tor' g hg
  exact ⟨N, c, fun n hn ↦ torMapVanishesAtSucc_of_tor_map_eq_zero _ t fun M ↦ h M n hn⟩

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0GA3, condition (3) of Tag 0G9V.** Let `I = (g 0, …, g (t - 1))` be an
ideal of a Noetherian ring `A` generated by at most `t` elements. There are `N` and `c`,
depending only on `A`, `I` and `t`, such that for every `n ≥ N` the transition
`A / I ^ n ↠ A / I ^ (n - c)` induces the zero map
`Ext ^ i (A / I ^ (n - c), M) → Ext ^ i (A / I ^ n, M)` for every module `M` and every `i > t`.

As `A` is Noetherian and `A / I ^ n` is a finite `A`-module, all seven conditions of
[Stacks, Tag 0G9V] are equivalent for the transition (`tfae_of_isNoetherianRing_of_finite`), so
this is the assertion that the transition satisfies them; it is obtained from condition (7),
`exists_uniform_torMapVanishesAtSucc_quotientFactor`. -/
@[stacks 0GA3 "condition (3) of Tag 0G9V"]
theorem exists_uniform_extMapVanishesAbove_quotientFactor [IsNoetherianRing A]
    {I : Ideal A} {t : ℕ} (g : Fin t → A) (hg : I = Ideal.span (Set.range g)) :
    ∃ N c : ℕ, ∀ n : ℕ, N ≤ n →
      ExtMapVanishesAbove
        (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c)))) t := by
  obtain ⟨N, c, h⟩ := exists_uniform_torMapVanishesAtSucc_quotientFactor g hg
  exact ⟨N, c, fun n hn ↦ extMapVanishesAbove_of_torMapVanishesAtSucc _ _ _ (h n hn)⟩

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0GA3, condition (1) of Tag 0G9V.** Let `I = (g 0, …, g (t - 1))` be an
ideal of a Noetherian ring `A` generated by at most `t` elements. There are `N` and `c`,
depending only on `A`, `I` and `t`, such that for every `n ≥ N` and every choice of projective
resolutions of `A / I ^ n` and of `A / I ^ (n - c)`, the transition `A / I ^ n ↠ A / I ^ (n - c)`
lifts to a map of resolutions whose components vanish in all homological degrees above `t`.

It is obtained from condition (7), `exists_uniform_torMapVanishesAtSucc_quotientFactor`, by the
equivalence of the conditions of [Stacks, Tag 0G9V] for a finite module over a Noetherian ring,
`tfae_of_isNoetherianRing_of_finite`. -/
@[stacks 0GA3 "condition (1) of Tag 0G9V"]
theorem exists_uniform_hasLiftVanishingAbove_quotientFactor [IsNoetherianRing A]
    {I : Ideal A} {t : ℕ} (g : Fin t → A) (hg : I = Ideal.span (Set.range g)) :
    ∃ N c : ℕ, ∀ n : ℕ, N ≤ n →
      ∀ {P P' : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A) ℤ}
        (p : P ⟶ singleComplex (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ n)))
        (p' : P' ⟶ singleComplex (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ (n - c))))
        [CochainComplex.IsProjectiveResolution p]
        [CochainComplex.IsProjectiveResolution p'],
        HasLiftVanishingAbove p p'
          (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
            (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c)))) t := by
  obtain ⟨N, c, h⟩ := exists_uniform_torMapVanishesAtSucc_quotientFactor g hg
  exact ⟨N, c, fun n hn _ _ p p' _ _ ↦
    ((tfae_of_isNoetherianRing_of_finite p p' _ t).out 7 1).1 (h n hn)⟩

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0GA3.** Let `I = (g 0, …, g (t - 1))` be an ideal of a Noetherian ring
`A` generated by at most `t` elements. There are `N` and `c`, depending only on `A`, `I` and `t`,
such that for every `n ≥ N` and every choice of projective resolutions of `A / I ^ n` and of
`A / I ^ (n - c)`, the transition `A / I ^ n ↠ A / I ^ (n - c)` satisfies all seven conditions of
[Stacks, Tag 0G9V] with `e = t`, in the order of the source: (1) a lift vanishing in all degrees
above `t`, (2) a lift vanishing in degree `t + 1`, (3) the zero map on `Ext ^ i` for all `i > t`,
(4) the zero map on `Ext ^ (t + 1)`, (5) the canonical class of degree `t + 1` pulls back to zero,
(6) the zero map on `Tor _ i` for all `i > t`, (7) the zero map on `Tor _ (t + 1)`.

All seven follow from condition (7), `exists_uniform_torMapVanishesAtSucc_quotientFactor`, by
`tfae_of_isNoetherianRing_of_finite`. -/
@[stacks 0GA3 "all seven conditions of Tag 0G9V at e = t"]
theorem exists_uniform_vanishingConditions_quotientFactor [IsNoetherianRing A]
    {I : Ideal A} {t : ℕ} (g : Fin t → A) (hg : I = Ideal.span (Set.range g)) :
    ∃ N c : ℕ, ∀ n : ℕ, N ≤ n →
      ∀ {P P' : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A) ℤ}
        (p : P ⟶ singleComplex (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ n)))
        (p' : P' ⟶ singleComplex (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ (n - c))))
        [CochainComplex.IsProjectiveResolution p]
        [CochainComplex.IsProjectiveResolution p'],
        let α := ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c)))
        HasLiftVanishingAbove p p' α t ∧ HasLiftVanishingAtSucc p p' α t ∧
          ExtMapVanishesAbove α t ∧ ExtMapVanishesAtSucc α t ∧
          CanonicalExtClassPullbackVanishes p p' α t ∧ TorMapVanishesAbove α t ∧
          TorMapVanishesAtSucc α t := by
  obtain ⟨N, c, h⟩ := exists_uniform_torMapVanishesAtSucc_quotientFactor g hg
  refine ⟨N, c, fun n hn _ _ p p' _ _ ↦ ?_⟩
  intro α
  have hT := tfae_of_isNoetherianRing_of_finite p p' α t
  have h7 : TorMapVanishesAtSucc α t := h n hn
  exact ⟨(hT.out 7 1).1 h7, (hT.out 7 2).1 h7, (hT.out 7 3).1 h7, (hT.out 7 4).1 h7,
    (hT.out 7 5).1 h7, (hT.out 7 6).1 h7, h7⟩

/-! ### Stacks tag 0GA3 at a level decoupled from the number of generators -/

/-- Let `I` be an ideal of a Noetherian ring `A` and let `e` be a degree above which a single
power of `I`, depending on `A` and `I` alone, annihilates `Tor _ i ^ A (M, A / I ^ q)` for every
`A`-module `M` and every `q`. There are `N` and `c` such that for every `n ≥ N` the transition
`A / I ^ n ↠ A / I ^ (n - c)` induces the zero map on `Tor _ (e + 1)` against every module.

The level `e` is the level of `hann` alone; it is unrelated to the number of generators of `I`,
which enters only the number of steps of the induction behind [Stacks, Tag 0GA2]. -/
theorem exists_uniform_torMapVanishesAtSucc_quotientFactor_of_annihilator_level
    [IsNoetherianRing A] (I : Ideal A) (e : ℕ)
    (hann : ∃ m : ℕ, ∀ (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (i q : ℕ), e < i →
      I ^ m ≤ Module.annihilator A
        (((Tor' (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).obj (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ q)))) :
    ∃ N c : ℕ, ∀ n : ℕ, N ≤ n →
      TorMapVanishesAtSucc
        (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c)))) e := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := hann
  obtain ⟨t, g, hg⟩ :=
    Submodule.fg_iff_exists_fin_generating_family.mp (IsNoetherian.noetherian I)
  obtain ⟨N, c, h⟩ :=
    exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_le_annihilator_level_tor' g hg.symm e m hm
  exact ⟨N, c, fun n hn ↦ torMapVanishesAtSucc_of_tor_map_eq_zero _ e fun M ↦ h M n hn⟩

/-- Let `I` be an ideal of a Noetherian ring `A` and let `e` be a degree above which a single
power of `I`, depending on `A` and `I` alone, annihilates `Tor _ i ^ A (M, A / I ^ q)` for every
`A`-module `M` and every `q`. There are `N` and `c` such that for every `n ≥ N` the transition
`A / I ^ n ↠ A / I ^ (n - c)` induces the zero map
`Ext ^ i (A / I ^ (n - c), M) → Ext ^ i (A / I ^ n, M)` for every module `M` and every `i > e`.

This is [Stacks, Tag 0GA3] with the degree `e = t` of its conclusion replaced by the level of
its hypothesis. -/
theorem exists_uniform_extMapVanishesAbove_quotientFactor_of_annihilator_level
    [IsNoetherianRing A] (I : Ideal A) (e : ℕ)
    (hann : ∃ m : ℕ, ∀ (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (i q : ℕ), e < i →
      I ^ m ≤ Module.annihilator A
        (((Tor' (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).obj (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ q)))) :
    ∃ N c : ℕ, ∀ n : ℕ, N ≤ n →
      ExtMapVanishesAbove
        (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c)))) e := by
  obtain ⟨N, c, h⟩ :=
    exists_uniform_torMapVanishesAtSucc_quotientFactor_of_annihilator_level I e hann
  exact ⟨N, c, fun n hn ↦ extMapVanishesAbove_of_torMapVanishesAtSucc _ _ _ (h n hn)⟩

end

end Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityII
